CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   On Mar 2, 2000 this sequence version replaced gi:32759.
CC   [2] also reports sequences for gamma-3, gamma-4, and a gamma
CC   pseudogene. Most of this sequence is 95% homologous with gamma-4.
CC   The hinge exons are only 70% homologous. The authors estimate that
CC   gamma-2 and gamma-4 diverged 6.6 million years ago. The authors in
CC   [1] speculate that intron-mediated domain transfer played an
CC   important role in the evolution of human gamma genes. They also
CC   report the hinge regions of gamma-1, gamma-3, gamma-4, and a
CC   pseudo-gamma gene. [1] estimates the divergence of the human gamma
CC   genes to be between 7.7 and 4.4 million years ago. This entry is
CC   part of a multigene region containing the gamma-2, gamma-4,
CC   epsilon-1, and alpha-2 genes. The relative locations of the four
CC   genes were determined by Flanagan and Rabbitts (Nature 300, 709-713
CC   (1982)). They refer to this gene group as region B. The region A
CC   genes are gamma-3, gamma-1, pseudo-epsilon, alpha-1. Flanagan and
CC   Rabbits also determined the general locations of the two regions.
CC   They place region A between the JH/mu/delta region and region B.
CC   Complete source information:
CC   Human fetal liver DNA, library of T. Maniatis [3] and Lawn et al
CC   [2],[1]; clones p-gamma-2RPA3 [2], 5A [3], and Ig-gamma-2-15 [1].
